       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Amlodipine 20 mg once daily is double the usual maximum of 10 mg per day. Doses above 10 mg raise the risk of peripheral edema, hypotension, and reflex tachycardia, and they add little blood-pressure benefit.\n\nWhich of these do you want?\n1. **Amlodipine 10 mg PO once daily.** This is the standard maximum dose. I can enter it now.\n2. **Amlodipine 5 mg PO once daily.** This is a typical starting dose, if the patient is starting therapy.\n3. **Amlodipine 20 mg PO once daily, as written.** If this is intentional, for example for a specific refractory indication, confirm and I'll enter it with a note that it exceeds the labeled maximum and was confirmed by you.\n\nIf BP isn't controlled on 10 mg, adding a second agent such as an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide-type diuretic is usually preferred to raising the amlodipine dose."
      }
     ],
